WEBVTT

00:01.660 --> 00:04.929
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.057 --> 00:08.359
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.411 --> 00:11.830
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.881 --> 00:14.800
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.825 --> 00:17.933
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.448 --> 00:21.600
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.668 --> 00:23.202
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.253 --> 00:24.604
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.688 --> 00:26.737
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.432 --> 00:36.533
Good morning.
I'm Tom Tucker.

00:36.600 --> 00:38.868
Coming up, we talk
to a man on the street

00:38.936 --> 00:41.504
while a man further back
on the street flips you off.

00:41.572 --> 00:44.073
But first, Quahog was hit by
a major blizzard last night.

00:44.141 --> 00:45.708
Here with more details
on the snowstorm

00:45.776 --> 00:47.477
is Asian correspondent
Tricia Nakahoma.

00:47.545 --> 00:49.479
That's wrong.
That's wrong.

00:49.547 --> 00:51.447
You're not doing
good so far.

00:51.515 --> 00:54.851
I'm standing here surrounded
by snowdrifts, stalled cars,

00:54.919 --> 00:56.819
and the one douchebag
who wears a tank top

00:56.887 --> 00:58.755
every time there's a blizzard.

00:58.822 --> 01:00.156
Yeah, this is nothin'.

01:00.224 --> 01:02.325
Guy at work drank a
quart of motor oil once

01:02.393 --> 01:03.760
and didn't even
die from it.

01:03.827 --> 01:05.578
Put that on the
news, but you won't.

01:05.646 --> 01:07.513
(laughter and excited chatter)

01:08.682 --> 01:10.016
Hey, guys, check it out.

01:10.100 --> 01:11.901
I peed my name in the snow.

01:14.138 --> 01:15.755
- Geez, Joe.
- That's normal.

01:15.823 --> 01:17.857
Wow, looks like the whole
neighborhood's out here.

01:17.942 --> 01:19.359
Yeah, I just hope
that weird albino

01:19.426 --> 01:20.793
up the street doesn't show up.

01:20.861 --> 01:22.095
That guy creeps me out.

01:22.162 --> 01:23.563
- Hello, Peter.
- Dah! Dah!

01:23.631 --> 01:25.381
H-Hey. Hey, Bill.

01:25.449 --> 01:27.467
What are you doing out
here in all this snow?

01:27.534 --> 01:29.335
Just taking my rabbit
to the vet.

01:31.622 --> 01:34.257
Well, I'm all done shoveling
your walk, Mr. Herbert.

01:34.325 --> 01:37.877
Thanks, Chris, but
there's some in here, too.

01:37.962 --> 01:40.196
BRIAN: Hey, check
it out-- lemon snow.

01:40.264 --> 01:41.881
- What?
- Yeah, that stuff's delicious.

01:41.949 --> 01:44.751
Lemon snow? You mean it just
falls from the sky like that?

01:44.818 --> 01:46.252
You bet. One of nature's treats.

01:46.320 --> 01:48.154
- You gonna have some?
- Nah, I'm already full.

01:48.222 --> 01:51.024
But you should have some before
the other kids get to it.

01:51.091 --> 01:52.392
What is it?
Like Italian ice?

01:52.459 --> 01:54.260
Yeah, exactly,
like a sorbet.

01:55.796 --> 01:57.130
Ugh! That's not lemon!

01:57.197 --> 01:58.798
- No, it's not.
- You bastard!

01:58.866 --> 02:01.901
I was having fun playing in the
snow, and now you've ruined it,

02:01.969 --> 02:03.603
like a pizza place
ruins a salad.

02:03.671 --> 02:05.138
Okay, four pizzas
and a salad.

02:05.205 --> 02:06.789
Salad? How do
you make a salad?

02:06.857 --> 02:09.025
First, you throw in
the whole head of lettuce.

02:09.093 --> 02:10.877
Even the hard-to-eat
white part at the bottom?

02:10.944 --> 02:12.779
That's what the people want!
Now, what else?

02:12.846 --> 02:14.564
I got a can of
whole black olives.

02:14.632 --> 02:15.815
Should I slice them up?

02:15.883 --> 02:17.917
What are you, crazy?
No, you keep 'em whole.

02:18.002 --> 02:20.603
You're gonna want to know you've
got an olive in your mouth.

02:20.671 --> 02:22.405
What about this tomato?
Cut it into thirds.

02:22.473 --> 02:25.008
It should be big enough
to pretend you've got red teeth.

02:25.075 --> 02:27.010
How about this carrot?
Should I cut it up?

02:27.061 --> 02:28.394
Yes, but very thin lengthwise.

02:28.479 --> 02:29.846
The whole length
of the carrot.

02:29.913 --> 02:32.098
One thin slice.
Okay, what else do we got?

02:32.182 --> 02:34.767
Well, we got these hot peppers,
but you can't really eat them.

02:34.835 --> 02:36.319
No problem. Dump 'em all in.

02:36.386 --> 02:38.104
Now, should we
put it in a bowl?

02:38.172 --> 02:39.939
No, let's put it
in a lasagna tray.

02:40.007 --> 02:41.341
Okay, great, I'll take it.

02:41.408 --> 02:43.710
Oh, and make sure to stick it
right on top of the pizzas

02:43.777 --> 02:45.445
so it stays nice and warm.

02:45.512 --> 02:46.496
(phone ringing)

02:46.563 --> 02:47.964
Hello, every pizza place.

02:51.268 --> 02:53.503
All right, Stewie, you
all set to spend the day

02:53.570 --> 02:54.787
with Grandma and Grandpa?

02:54.855 --> 02:56.506
Ugh, I hate being around
old people.

02:56.573 --> 02:59.075
They've always got weird stuff
in their refrigerator.

02:59.126 --> 03:00.977
Ah, I'm hungry.
What do we got?

03:01.045 --> 03:03.946
Let's see. Eye drops,
baking soda and some film.

03:04.014 --> 03:05.481
OLD MAN:
Close the door.

03:05.549 --> 03:07.917
You're running up
long distance charges!

03:07.985 --> 03:09.886
(doorbell rings)

03:09.953 --> 03:11.738
Ah, sorry.
Thought I had more time.

03:11.805 --> 03:13.373
Hi, Daddy.
Stewie's all ready.

03:13.440 --> 03:14.741
You boys have fun.

03:14.808 --> 03:16.476
There's my little guy.

03:16.543 --> 03:19.145
♪ Well, Grandpa's here. ♪

03:19.213 --> 03:20.847
Oh, God, it's
the song again.

03:20.914 --> 03:22.198
♪ Yes, Grandpa's here! ♪

03:22.266 --> 03:24.083
It doesn't even
rhyme at all.

03:24.151 --> 03:27.553
♪ He's going to buy you a soda
and drive you around. ♪

03:27.621 --> 03:28.988
Let's go.

03:32.159 --> 03:33.793
(radio static)

03:33.877 --> 03:37.163
Hey, just so you know, we're not
listening to a radio station.

03:37.247 --> 03:40.083
We're listening to the hiss
between two radio stations.

03:40.134 --> 03:41.751
(tires squealing)

03:41.802 --> 03:43.669
Whoa. Watch your driving!

03:45.472 --> 03:47.456
Is he... Is he sleeping?

03:47.508 --> 03:49.759
Hey! Hey, wake up! Wake up!

03:49.810 --> 03:51.177
You, lady, wake him up!

03:51.261 --> 03:53.479
<i>You like the Tom and Jerry,
do you, dear?</i>

03:53.564 --> 03:55.798
Well, we'll dial them up
when we get home.

03:55.849 --> 03:58.017
What the hell are you talking
about?! We're about to...

03:59.903 --> 04:01.170
(groans)

04:01.238 --> 04:02.405
What happened?

04:02.473 --> 04:04.207
Where are my
knitting needles?

04:06.677 --> 04:09.145
(gasps)
Goodness, dear, I'm so sorry.

04:09.213 --> 04:11.313
No worries.
Now I can work at Hot Topic

04:11.365 --> 04:13.616
and make people sick
as I ring up their purchases.

04:13.684 --> 04:15.501
(tires screeching)

04:21.725 --> 04:24.010
Oh, damn it.

04:24.094 --> 04:25.478
Dude, bad news.

04:25.546 --> 04:26.746
You're dead.

04:26.814 --> 04:28.564
What? But I'm Death!

04:28.632 --> 04:30.166
Sorry, dude.
Super Death.

04:30.234 --> 04:31.500
You're done.

04:31.552 --> 04:33.269
So what now?
I go to Heaven?

04:33.337 --> 04:35.571
Nope, when a Death dies,
he gets reincarnated.

04:35.639 --> 04:39.642
You're being reincarnated as
a Chinese baby right... now!

04:39.710 --> 04:42.111
(whirring)

04:42.179 --> 04:43.913
- Girl?
- Girl.

04:45.082 --> 04:46.582
Oh, no!

04:46.650 --> 04:49.118
The egg that I was supposed
to take care of

04:49.186 --> 04:50.686
for my high school project!

04:50.754 --> 04:52.188
Mr. Burke was right.

04:52.256 --> 04:54.290
I'm not ready to be a parent.

04:54.358 --> 04:55.541
Wait a minute.

04:55.609 --> 04:57.210
I'm not in high school anymore.

04:57.277 --> 04:59.579
Maybe this is all a dream.

04:59.646 --> 05:01.747
<i>Aah! It was a dream!</i>

05:01.815 --> 05:03.716
I need a glass of water.

05:03.801 --> 05:05.318
Wait a minute.

05:05.385 --> 05:07.587
I moved out of the desert
years ago.

05:07.654 --> 05:09.489
<i>Maybe this is a dream!</i>

05:09.556 --> 05:11.324
Aah!

05:11.391 --> 05:12.892
Phew.

05:12.960 --> 05:15.428
<i>I am ready
to be a parent, Mr. Burke.</i>

05:19.433 --> 05:21.501
Daddy, I'm so happy
you're all right.

05:21.568 --> 05:23.369
We're lucky
it wasn't more serious.

05:23.437 --> 05:25.521
Hey, how's
the old guy doing?

05:25.572 --> 05:26.856
Ugh, now here's Joe.

05:26.924 --> 05:28.991
Why is everybody
we know depressing?

05:29.059 --> 05:31.761
Mr. Pewterschmidt, I'm afraid
I have some bad news.

05:31.829 --> 05:33.830
I'm gonna have to revoke
your driver's license.

05:33.897 --> 05:35.231
What?!

05:35.299 --> 05:37.533
It's obvious your advanced age
has impaired your ability

05:37.601 --> 05:39.068
to drive safely.

05:39.136 --> 05:41.070
Please, Joe, I know he had
an accident,

05:41.138 --> 05:42.738
but can't you look the
other way

05:42.806 --> 05:44.407
this one time
as a friend?

05:44.474 --> 05:46.442
Yeah, you know, Joe,
you owe this family.

05:46.510 --> 05:49.478
I didn't tell anyone about
your Fiona Apple tribute video.

05:49.546 --> 05:50.880
♪ ♪

05:50.931 --> 05:54.767
♪ I've been a bad, bad girl ♪

05:56.537 --> 06:01.691
♪ I've been careless
with a delicate man ♪

06:01.758 --> 06:05.427
♪ And it's a sad, sad world ♪

06:07.064 --> 06:10.816
♪ When a girl will break a boy,
just because she can. ♪

06:10.901 --> 06:12.118
I'm brok.
(door rattling)

06:12.185 --> 06:14.003
BONNIE:
Joe, open the garage.

06:14.071 --> 06:16.539
I've earned this private time!

06:16.607 --> 06:18.274
Listen, I don't
have time for this.

06:18.325 --> 06:20.526
I'm late for a hostile
takeover of a jelly factory.

06:20.594 --> 06:22.361
I'll show those Smuckers.

06:22.429 --> 06:24.664
That's fine,
but you can't drive.

06:24.731 --> 06:26.098
Oh, don't be
ridiculous!

06:26.166 --> 06:27.750
Driver Pete at
your service, sir.

06:27.818 --> 06:29.485
- Peter, we're not doing that.
- Aw.

06:29.553 --> 06:31.554
Carter, you work
too much as it is.

06:31.621 --> 06:33.372
You're not a young
man anymore.

06:33.440 --> 06:35.041
You need to slow down.

06:35.108 --> 06:36.776
Slow down?! I
can't slow down.

06:36.843 --> 06:38.444
I'm running a six-billion-
dollar company.

06:38.512 --> 06:40.730
If I slow down, the
company goes under.

06:40.797 --> 06:42.465
It just seems
to me that perhaps

06:42.532 --> 06:45.201
it's time to think
about retirement.

06:45.269 --> 06:47.103
Never! Retirement's
for old people.

06:47.170 --> 06:48.738
I can work till I die.

06:48.805 --> 06:50.122
Maybe even after that.

06:50.190 --> 06:51.624
Mr. Pewterschmidt, the
gentlemen from Zurich

06:51.692 --> 06:53.492
are here for your 10:00.

06:56.029 --> 06:58.164
Will you need
anything else?

06:58.231 --> 07:00.249
Mr. Pewterschmidt!

07:00.317 --> 07:02.485
<i>But, dear, we are old.</i>

07:02.552 --> 07:05.004
We can't keep pretending
that nothing's changed.

07:05.072 --> 07:07.640
I mean, we almost injured
our grandchild today.

07:07.708 --> 07:09.475
Besides, you're always
complaining

07:09.543 --> 07:11.911
that you don't have
enough time to play polo

07:11.979 --> 07:14.680
or sit in a chair
and moisten your mouth.

07:14.748 --> 07:16.215
That is true.

07:16.283 --> 07:18.935
It does sometimes take me
a while to moisten my mouth.

07:25.759 --> 07:27.810
There we go, all moist.

07:27.878 --> 07:29.245
You see, dear?

07:29.313 --> 07:30.579
And that's only
the beginning.

07:30.647 --> 07:32.865
Retirement will be
a wonderful adventure,

07:32.933 --> 07:34.200
and we'll do it together.

07:34.267 --> 07:35.501
You're gonna retire?

07:35.569 --> 07:36.669
From what?

07:36.737 --> 07:38.471
There, isn't it fun already?

07:38.538 --> 07:39.805
(sighs)

07:39.873 --> 07:42.508
Okay. I'll retire.

07:42.576 --> 07:45.144
Oh, Daddy, I think
that's for the best.

07:45.212 --> 07:47.580
I need a doctor!
Is there a doctor?!

07:54.325 --> 07:56.860
<i>ANNOUNCER: We now return to
The Superfriends' Accountant.</i>

07:56.928 --> 07:58.629
Look, you guys
are hemorrhaging money.

07:58.696 --> 08:00.831
This Hall of Justice is sitting
on five acres

08:00.899 --> 08:01.865
of commercial real estate.

08:01.933 --> 08:03.100
How do you afford this?

08:03.167 --> 08:04.401
We're the Superfriends.

08:04.469 --> 08:06.270
Yeah, but you guys
have no income.

08:06.337 --> 08:08.605
You owe four million dollars
in back property taxes.

08:08.673 --> 08:10.507
We fight evil
wherever we find it.

08:10.592 --> 08:12.092
Well, that's not
gonna be enough.

08:12.160 --> 08:13.794
Look, you may
need to reach out

08:13.861 --> 08:15.946
to some wealthy benefactors
for financial backing.

08:16.014 --> 08:17.881
Do any of you know
billionaire Bruce Wayne?

08:17.949 --> 08:19.383
No. None of us do.

08:19.450 --> 08:21.919
And he wouldn't want to lend
us money anyway... I hear.

08:21.986 --> 08:23.453
Hey, hey, hey!

08:23.521 --> 08:26.156
What's up, Ginas...
'g-'ginas... vaginas?

08:26.224 --> 08:27.057
What's up,
vaginas?!

08:27.125 --> 08:28.292
Ah-ha, gotcha!

08:28.359 --> 08:29.977
Mr. Pewterschmidt,
what are you doing here?

08:30.044 --> 08:32.813
I'm retired now. Got
a lot of free time.

08:32.880 --> 08:34.531
So what do you guys
do here?

08:34.616 --> 08:37.034
Well, we usually just sit here
and complain about our lives.

08:37.101 --> 08:39.536
Like this morning, Lois was such
a pain in the ass...

08:39.604 --> 08:41.705
Hey! That's my daughter
you're talking about!

08:41.773 --> 08:44.574
Oh. I mean this, um,
redheaded lady

08:44.642 --> 08:48.178
who lives in my bed was a real
pain in the ass this morning.

08:48.246 --> 08:49.746
Oh, she sounds like a bitch.

08:49.814 --> 08:50.914
Yeah, what a bitch.

08:50.982 --> 08:52.115
Bitchazoid, right, guys?

08:52.183 --> 08:53.684
Yeah. I hope you're doing her.

08:53.751 --> 08:54.584
Oh, big time.

08:54.652 --> 08:56.119
Yeah, that's hot.

08:56.187 --> 08:57.788
That's hot. I'm gonna think
about that tonight.

08:57.855 --> 08:59.840
Oh, we do all kinds
of crazy stuff.

08:59.907 --> 09:01.642
Sometimes
we even have phone sax.

09:01.709 --> 09:02.976
<i>Don't you mean
phone sex?</i>

09:03.044 --> 09:04.544
<i>No, Joe.
Phone sax.</i>

09:04.612 --> 09:05.912
Are you ready?

09:05.980 --> 09:07.748
You better believe it.

09:07.815 --> 09:09.666
(playing "Baker Street")

09:15.740 --> 09:17.424
Oh, Peter!

09:17.492 --> 09:19.593
Yeah. Now your turn.

09:19.661 --> 09:21.395
And do it how I like.

09:21.462 --> 09:23.680
(giggles)
Okay.

09:23.748 --> 09:25.615
(playing intro to
"You Can Call Me Al")

09:30.905 --> 09:33.840
Yeah. Don't wash
the mouthpiece.

09:37.211 --> 09:38.712
Good news, guys.

09:38.780 --> 09:40.180
Now that Grandpa's retired,

09:40.248 --> 09:42.316
he's gonna have more time
to spend with us.

09:42.383 --> 09:43.350
ALL:
Oh!

09:43.418 --> 09:44.918
We don't want to do that, Mom.

09:44.986 --> 09:47.004
Yeah, all he ever does is
ask you what you want to do

09:47.071 --> 09:49.239
so he can shoot it down and
tell you what he wants to do.

09:49.307 --> 09:50.407
Hey, there's
my family!

09:50.475 --> 09:52.642
So, what do you guys
want to do today?

09:52.710 --> 09:54.411
I'd like to go
to the mall, Grandpa.

09:54.479 --> 09:55.645
No parking at the mall.

09:55.713 --> 09:57.114
It's a terrible place.
What else?

09:57.181 --> 09:58.215
Um, how about
the zoo?

09:58.282 --> 09:59.616
Too much walking.
Too much noise.

09:59.701 --> 10:01.018
You can't have
any good conversation.

10:01.085 --> 10:02.252
Not like at Chili's.
Where else?

10:02.320 --> 10:03.587
Well, there's always the beach.

10:03.654 --> 10:05.789
No, you got to sit
on the ground to eat.

10:05.857 --> 10:08.191
I need a cushioned chair with
back support like at Chili's.

10:08.259 --> 10:10.577
Okay, well...
how about Chili's?

10:10.645 --> 10:12.062
Maybe, maybe.

10:12.130 --> 10:13.630
Let's get in the car
and see where it takes us.

10:15.199 --> 10:17.167
(rings doorbell)

10:17.235 --> 10:18.602
Hey, Carter.

10:18.669 --> 10:19.936
Hello, Quandary.

10:20.004 --> 10:21.104
It's, uh...
It's Quagmire.

10:21.172 --> 10:22.472
You looking for Peter?

10:22.540 --> 10:23.907
No, he's at work. Lame.

10:23.975 --> 10:25.425
Oh. Well, what
do you want?

10:25.493 --> 10:27.294
I hear you're kind of
a cool guy.

10:27.362 --> 10:28.779
Thought maybe
we could hang out.

10:28.846 --> 10:30.180
Uh... okay.

10:30.248 --> 10:32.015
Okay! Carter and Quandary,
hanging out.

10:32.083 --> 10:35.385
All right, I just got to go take
a misty, stop-and-go piss

10:35.453 --> 10:37.621
in your bathroom,
then we'll be good to go.

10:42.760 --> 10:44.742
Lois, how the hell much
longer is your dad gonna

10:44.767 --> 10:45.967
be hanging around here?

10:46.130 --> 10:48.348
- He's starting to drive me crazy.
- (sighs) I know, Peter,

10:48.416 --> 10:50.834
but he's my father and I
don't know what else to do.

10:50.902 --> 10:52.936
Well, I don't know how
much more I can take.

10:53.004 --> 10:54.704
I can't even get
any sleep with him here.

10:56.641 --> 10:58.008
Hey.

10:58.076 --> 11:00.277
- Hey.
- Wha-Wha-Wha-Wha- What is it?

11:00.344 --> 11:02.579
I can't sleep.
I'm scared of ghosts.

11:02.647 --> 11:04.698
Carter, there's
no such thing as ghosts.

11:04.766 --> 11:06.133
Are you sure?

11:06.200 --> 11:08.468
<i>Well, now I'm not.
Come on, get in here!</i>

11:09.704 --> 11:10.871
It's safe under
here, right?

11:10.938 --> 11:12.606
I think so,
but I'm not sure.

11:12.673 --> 11:14.841
I just recently started
believing in ghosts.

11:17.745 --> 11:19.579
Hi, Mom. Hi, Daddy.

11:19.647 --> 11:22.115
Lois! What are
you two doing here?

11:22.183 --> 11:24.418
Well, we wanted to talk
to you about something.

11:24.485 --> 11:25.719
Hmm. What's that?

11:25.787 --> 11:27.187
Well, we were just thinking,

11:27.255 --> 11:30.190
now that Daddy's retired
that you and he might be happier

11:30.258 --> 11:33.160
in a place where you can be
with people your own age.

11:33.227 --> 11:35.395
You know, make some new friends.

11:35.463 --> 11:36.244
What are you talking about?

11:36.269 --> 11:38.298
Well, we actually
brought you a few brochures

11:38.299 --> 11:40.600
of some lovely retirement
communities in Florida.

11:40.668 --> 11:42.202
And I helped.

11:42.270 --> 11:43.303
Florida?!

11:43.328 --> 11:45.439
Mm, this one's even
got the word "sunset"

11:45.440 --> 11:47.307
four times in
the name of it.

11:47.375 --> 11:49.876
Huh. These people are
biking without helmets.

11:49.944 --> 11:51.812
Must be a pretty
kick-back place.

11:51.879 --> 11:53.563
These actually
look quite nice,

11:53.631 --> 11:56.933
and we could finally get away
from these dreadful winters.

11:57.001 --> 11:59.002
Yeah. We'll even help you
move in and get settled.

11:59.070 --> 12:01.354
Wait a minute, why would
I want to live in Florida?

12:01.405 --> 12:03.223
Black people's votes go
right in the garbage.

12:03.291 --> 12:04.674
All right!
We're moving to Florida!

12:04.742 --> 12:07.110
Oh, Carter,
this is wonderful!

12:07.178 --> 12:09.012
Aw, look at
that smile, Lois.

12:09.080 --> 12:10.879
Reminds of that guy
who was way too happy he

12:10.904 --> 12:12.567
didn't get killed on 9/11.

12:12.717 --> 12:15.118
(gasping): I'm ten minutes
late for work!

12:15.186 --> 12:17.137
Look at that!
I stayed up late

12:17.205 --> 12:19.673
<i>watching Monday Night Football
and that saved my life, huh?</i>

12:19.740 --> 12:20.907
Isn't that awesome?

12:20.975 --> 12:23.109
Oh, but oh...

12:30.852 --> 12:32.185
Hi there. Welcome.

12:32.253 --> 12:34.237
I'm Ryan, the manager
here at Oceanside,

12:34.305 --> 12:36.072
and I'll be showing
you around today.

12:36.140 --> 12:37.474
First question, though:

12:37.542 --> 12:39.876
are you two old enough
to be here?

12:39.944 --> 12:41.244
(giggles):
Oh, dear!

12:41.312 --> 12:42.946
(laughs)
I like you, Ryan.

12:43.014 --> 12:44.014
You're cool.

12:48.402 --> 12:51.121
Over there is our statue
of Angela Lansbury.

12:53.324 --> 12:56.026
Protect us, oh, Lansbury,
from rude teenagers,

12:56.093 --> 12:59.129
from soup that is both
too hot and too cold,

12:59.197 --> 13:02.432
and from anyone who calls,
but please have people call.

13:05.219 --> 13:06.870
Our state-of-the-art movie
theater is equipped

13:06.938 --> 13:09.806
with some terrific innovations
to cater to our residents,

13:09.874 --> 13:12.576
including a button on every seat
that will pause the film

13:12.643 --> 13:14.411
whenever anyone
has a question.

13:14.478 --> 13:15.979
Hey, guys.

13:16.047 --> 13:18.949
MAN: Why is he blue now?
Is it cold on that planet?

13:19.016 --> 13:20.483
MAN 2:
Why are they mumbling?

13:20.551 --> 13:22.252
Why does everyone
in pictures today mumble?

13:22.320 --> 13:23.353
I can't hear!

13:23.421 --> 13:24.955
♪ ♪

13:25.022 --> 13:26.623
MAN 3:
Is that Sig-nory Weaver?

13:26.691 --> 13:28.358
WOMAN:
That's not how you say it.

13:28.426 --> 13:30.160
MAN 3:
Well, she shouldn't be smoking.

13:30.228 --> 13:33.029
She's a handsome woman,
and that'll ruin her fast.

13:33.097 --> 13:34.364
♪ ♪

13:34.432 --> 13:37.167
MAN 4: Is Unobtainium
very easy to obtain?

13:37.235 --> 13:38.835
Well, I hope you
enjoyed the tour.

13:38.903 --> 13:40.303
Oh, yeah, it was great.

13:40.371 --> 13:42.872
Except for that lady who
kept yelling "Byaah! Byaah!"

13:42.940 --> 13:45.258
Well, we'll just need you
to fill out this paperwork,

13:45.326 --> 13:47.994
and then we'll get you
moved into your condo.

13:48.045 --> 13:49.930
Oh, isn't this
wonderful, dear!

13:49.997 --> 13:51.915
No! No, it's not
wonderful at all!

13:51.983 --> 13:54.017
There's no way in hell
I'm gonna live here!

13:54.085 --> 13:58.238
This place is nothing but old
people marching to their deaths!

13:58.306 --> 14:00.490
You hear me?
I'm not one of you!

14:00.558 --> 14:02.492
And I never will be!

14:05.212 --> 14:06.680
Hey, look, it's
old man Withers,

14:06.747 --> 14:08.531
the guy who owns
the amusement park!

14:08.599 --> 14:10.850
<i>But let's see who's
really under there.</i>

14:10.901 --> 14:12.185
(screams)
(gasps)

14:12.253 --> 14:13.420
A skeleton!

14:13.487 --> 14:15.522
- Can I have my face back?
- No!

14:15.590 --> 14:16.957
You're going to jail!

14:24.601 --> 14:25.902
Oh, this is dreadful.

14:25.969 --> 14:28.671
I thought Carter and I were
going to be so happy here.

14:28.739 --> 14:31.107
I'll tell you what, Babs,
let me have a talk with him.

14:32.309 --> 14:33.609
Hey there, buddy.

14:33.677 --> 14:34.877
Go away!

14:34.945 --> 14:37.813
You know, you remind
me of a guy I know.

14:37.881 --> 14:40.650
This guy worked and worked
and never wanted to retire,

14:40.717 --> 14:43.419
even though it would've been
the best thing for him.

14:43.487 --> 14:45.421
You know what that
man's name was?

14:45.489 --> 14:47.323
Jon Benet Ramsey.

14:48.525 --> 14:49.892
I-I-I think.

14:49.960 --> 14:51.494
I think that's the guy.

14:51.561 --> 14:53.396
- What?
- You're darn right what.

14:53.463 --> 14:55.231
Now, let's get
back in there.

14:55.299 --> 14:57.900
Peter, get lost! I'm not gonna
retire, and that's that!

14:57.968 --> 15:00.536
Come on, Carter, everybody's
got to retire at some point.

15:00.604 --> 15:02.571
Like that drill sergeant
with Alzheimer's.

15:03.740 --> 15:05.574
Looks like we got
a joker here.

15:05.642 --> 15:06.909
What's your
name, soldier?

15:06.977 --> 15:08.377
Sir, McArdle, sir!

15:08.445 --> 15:09.645
Well, no (bleep)!

15:09.713 --> 15:12.148
You look like some
kind of joker to me.

15:12.215 --> 15:13.249
What's your
name, soldier?

15:13.317 --> 15:14.717
Sir, McArdle, sir!

15:14.785 --> 15:16.619
Are you (bleep) me?

15:16.687 --> 15:18.254
Probably some
kind of joker.

15:18.322 --> 15:19.622
What's your
name, soldier?

15:19.690 --> 15:20.990
Sir, McArdle, sir!

15:21.058 --> 15:22.792
Well, la-dee (bleep) da!

15:22.859 --> 15:25.795
I guess we got some
kind of joker here!

15:25.862 --> 15:27.997
Look, Carter, I'll
make a deal with you.

15:28.065 --> 15:30.145
You give me just one day
to show you how great retired

15:30.170 --> 15:31.610
life can be for an old fella,

15:32.302 --> 15:34.337
and I'll let you honk
the horn one time.

15:34.404 --> 15:36.038
- Really?
- Uh-huh.

15:36.106 --> 15:37.540
(honks)

15:37.607 --> 15:39.375
(giggles) I'm pretending
there's traffic.

15:39.443 --> 15:40.776
There you go, that's...

15:40.844 --> 15:43.346
- Once!
- God, I wasn't even gonna do it!

15:46.233 --> 15:47.700
So, how do you
win this game?

15:47.768 --> 15:49.935
Just fill this out when they
say the letter and the numbers?

15:50.003 --> 15:51.103
Eh, that's a sucker's bet.

15:51.171 --> 15:52.855
There's only one way
to win this game--

15:52.923 --> 15:54.957
wait for someone else to win
and steal his card.

15:55.025 --> 15:56.759
G-27.

15:56.827 --> 15:58.227
Bingo!

15:58.295 --> 16:00.629
- It's go time.
- What do we do, sneak up behind him?

16:00.697 --> 16:02.515
No, he's got cataracts.
Follow my lead.

16:04.051 --> 16:05.151
(loud thud)

16:07.070 --> 16:08.604
Bingo, bitches!

16:10.090 --> 16:11.257
Bingo.

16:15.996 --> 16:17.496
All right, Carter,
now that you're retired,

16:17.581 --> 16:19.114
you're gonna need a
whole new wardrobe.

16:19.166 --> 16:22.418
And what better place to start
than the Slightly Open Robery?

16:22.486 --> 16:24.203
♪ Hey, hobo man ♪

16:24.271 --> 16:28.107
♪ Hey, Dapper Dan,
you've both got your style ♪

16:28.175 --> 16:30.142
♪ But, brother,
you're never fully dressed ♪

16:30.210 --> 16:32.511
♪ Without a smile... ♪

16:33.714 --> 16:35.681
Yes. The penis one.

16:37.317 --> 16:39.018
All right, Mr. Pewterschmidt,
now, you know how

16:39.086 --> 16:40.319
in your building
your office temperature

16:40.387 --> 16:41.954
was controlled
by a central air system

16:42.022 --> 16:44.523
that you had nothing to do with?
Yeah, I hated that.

16:44.591 --> 16:47.059
Well, check it out-- this room
has its very own thermostat

16:47.127 --> 16:48.494
that you can fiddle with.
- Really?

16:48.562 --> 16:50.112
I can change the
temperature in here?

16:50.163 --> 16:52.081
You're retired-- you
can do anything you want.

16:52.149 --> 16:54.316
Well, I am kind of warm.
I'll try it out.

16:54.367 --> 16:56.135
Oh, that's perfect.

16:56.203 --> 16:58.788
Now I'm cold.
Crank up the thermostat.

16:58.855 --> 17:00.456
Ah, wonderful.

17:00.524 --> 17:02.091
Hotter than
blazes in here.

17:02.159 --> 17:04.443
But wait-- I can
turn the heat down.

17:04.511 --> 17:05.711
(whispers):
He's learning.

17:07.514 --> 17:08.731
Bye, you guys.

17:08.799 --> 17:10.499
We'll be down
to visit real soon.

17:10.567 --> 17:13.018
Mr. Pewterschmidt, I'm glad you
finally came around about this place.

17:13.086 --> 17:15.304
Peter, I got to admit,
it's not bad at all.

17:15.372 --> 17:17.173
Never thought I'd get
used to the idea

17:17.240 --> 17:19.942
of giving up work and just
devoting my life to leisure.

17:20.010 --> 17:22.695
I guess this is what people
mean by the word "relax."

17:22.763 --> 17:23.896
Take care, dear.

17:23.964 --> 17:25.865
We'll see you soon.
Yeah, have fun.

17:25.932 --> 17:28.400
Just remember not to go out
into actual Florida.

17:28.468 --> 17:30.336
You don't want
to meet those people.

17:30.403 --> 17:31.670
(doorbell rings)

17:31.738 --> 17:33.739
Hi. I just moved
into the neighborhood,

17:33.807 --> 17:37.243
and I'm required by law to inform
you that I am a sex offender.

17:37.310 --> 17:39.245
Oh, don't worry
about it-- so am I.

17:39.312 --> 17:40.880
This whole block
is S.O.'s.

17:40.947 --> 17:43.949
We use the abbreviation "S.O's"
because it saves a lot of time

17:44.017 --> 17:46.585
over saying "Sex Offender," because
that's all we talk about.

17:46.653 --> 17:48.654
Well, I'm also into football.
Don't care.

17:48.722 --> 17:51.290
No time for F.B.
All about S.O.

17:51.358 --> 17:54.360
Make no mistake, Florida
is the South's trash can.

17:58.999 --> 18:00.800
Boy, these eggs
are delicious.

18:00.867 --> 18:02.134
Good job, Lois.

18:02.202 --> 18:03.853
Good job, local hen.

18:03.920 --> 18:05.721
Aw, bucka bucka baw.

18:05.789 --> 18:07.656
(phone rings)

18:07.724 --> 18:09.258
Hello?

18:09.326 --> 18:10.693
Hi, Mom.

18:10.760 --> 18:11.861
What?

18:11.928 --> 18:13.529
Oh, my God!

18:13.597 --> 18:16.699
Oh, my God, o-okay, we'll be
down there as soon as we can.

18:16.766 --> 18:17.950
Mom, what's wrong?

18:18.018 --> 18:19.385
We're going
to Florida.

18:19.452 --> 18:20.753
Why? What happened?

18:20.821 --> 18:22.955
There's something horribly wrong
with your grandpa.

18:28.912 --> 18:30.229
Oh, Lois!

18:30.297 --> 18:32.198
I'm so glad
you made it.

18:32.265 --> 18:34.366
He's been like this for days.

18:34.434 --> 18:36.068
Oh, my God!

18:36.136 --> 18:37.269
(grumbling)

18:37.337 --> 18:38.771
...cream of wheat.

18:38.839 --> 18:40.039
(mumbling)

18:40.106 --> 18:41.140
<i>...Jeopardy.</i>

18:41.208 --> 18:42.708
(mumbling)

18:42.776 --> 18:44.310
...butterscotch pudding.

18:44.377 --> 18:45.311
This is awful!

18:45.378 --> 18:46.779
What's happened to him?

18:46.847 --> 18:48.514
I don't know, dear.

18:48.582 --> 18:51.750
He sleeps 18 hours a day,
he refuses to bathe,

18:51.818 --> 18:53.853
and he's stopped
making any sense.

18:53.920 --> 18:55.616
Aw, that sounds like
the sad little fat girl

18:55.641 --> 18:57.241
who lives in all of us

18:57.324 --> 18:58.624
and is struggling
to get out.

18:58.692 --> 19:00.392
(muffled grunts)

19:00.460 --> 19:02.161
Did my parents
call yet?

19:02.229 --> 19:04.096
Nobody's looking for you!
Now, stay in there!

19:04.164 --> 19:06.265
Sometimes she tries
to get out the other way.

19:06.333 --> 19:08.367
That's why I keep
a cork in my bum.

19:08.435 --> 19:09.869
Daddy?

19:09.936 --> 19:11.971
Daddy, can you hear me?

19:12.038 --> 19:14.373
Oh, God, we should never
have brought him here.

19:14.441 --> 19:15.574
You're right, dear.

19:15.642 --> 19:18.043
I can't stand
to see him like this.

19:18.111 --> 19:19.578
Well, we got
to do something.

19:19.646 --> 19:22.348
Don't worry, you guys, I think
I might know how to fix this.

19:22.415 --> 19:25.451
But first look-- I turned
him into Groucho Marx.

19:25.518 --> 19:27.786
That's hilarious.

19:31.124 --> 19:33.475
Peter, what is this
supposed to accomplish?

19:33.526 --> 19:35.678
Don't you see, Lois?
When we forced him to retire,

19:35.745 --> 19:37.580
we took all the challenge
out of his life.

19:37.647 --> 19:40.249
Perhaps some people aren't
meant to retire at all.

19:40.317 --> 19:43.535
Exactly! Now, let's see if we
can put some fire back into him.

19:43.620 --> 19:46.622
Margot, it's time to take this
company in a new direction--

19:46.690 --> 19:49.475
starting with being honest with
the IRS about our profits.

19:49.542 --> 19:51.627
(mumbling)

19:51.695 --> 19:54.129
We're also gonna stop
reading employee e-mails.

19:54.197 --> 19:56.565
<i>(mumbling)
...our servers.</i>

19:56.633 --> 19:58.400
And from now on it's
against the rules

19:58.468 --> 20:00.586
to pat female employees
on the fanny.

20:00.654 --> 20:03.439
(mumbling):
...like touching butts!

20:03.506 --> 20:05.507
And tell the African-American
elevator attendant

20:05.575 --> 20:07.376
he no longer has to
wear white gloves.

20:07.444 --> 20:10.529
Why don't you just tell him
he can sleep with my wife, too?!

20:10.614 --> 20:11.614
Daddy!

20:11.681 --> 20:13.065
Oh, Carter!
You're back!

20:13.133 --> 20:14.850
You're damn
right I am!

20:14.918 --> 20:16.663
Don't you ever try to
stick me in one of those

20:16.688 --> 20:18.300
retirement places again!

20:18.888 --> 20:22.224
I plan on sitting behind this desk
until the day I die.

20:22.292 --> 20:24.260
Getting old is right
for some people,

20:24.327 --> 20:26.595
but not for me.
- I know, Daddy.

20:26.663 --> 20:28.714
You were right,
and we're sorry.

20:28.782 --> 20:30.716
(phone rings)

20:30.784 --> 20:32.217
Hey, Mom.

20:32.285 --> 20:34.653
No, Mom, you're staying
in the nursing home.

20:34.721 --> 20:36.722
I... I don't care.

20:36.790 --> 20:38.324
I-I don't care.

20:38.391 --> 20:41.060
M-Mom, believe me, no one
is touching you in your sleep.

20:41.127 --> 20:42.561
'Cause you're gross.

20:42.629 --> 20:44.346
And even if they are, so what,
who are you saving yourself for?

20:45.941 --> 20:48.656
Hey, look, I-I got to go.
I don't know if we're coming

20:48.657 --> 20:51.141
to Thanksgiving.
Because I don't know!

20:51.854 --> 20:54.055
- She's staying in there.
- I know.

20:54.056 --> 21:55.156
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru